// ALICE coherent rho0 photoproduction in PbPb at sqrt(sNN) = 5.02 TeV
// [REFERENCE: arXiv:2002.10897, Sec. 3.3 and Table 4]
// The observable is the fitted rho Breit-Wigner contribution integrated from 2 m_pi to m_rho + 5 Gamma_rho
// HEPData d sigma/dy is folded to d sigma/d|y|, including both rapidity signs
// Coherent refers to rho production on the whole nucleus, additional photon exchanges can emit neutrons
// 0n0n has no forward neutrons, 0nXn includes either one-sided orientation, XnXn has neutrons on both sides
// Total is neutron-inclusive coherent production, not coherent plus incoherent production
// The total overlaps the exclusive classes and is excluded from their combined fit
// Predictions use optical ion survival and ordinary Glauber shadowing
